@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: how one subagent body reaches four harnesses that disagree on frontmatter
' covers: defs/subagents/**
' covers: defs/lib/render-subagents.sh
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/contract/agents_shared_test.go
' covers: defs/*/defaults/agents/**
' covers: defs/*/*/defaults/agents/**
'
' ── SUBAGENTS ARE NOT BAKED AS FILES ───────────────────────────────────────
' One body per agent lives in /opt/proveo/subagents, and the entrypoint
' composes them per harness at start (proveo_seed <harness> → render_subagents)
' into the harness's own agents directory — for cecli, $CECLI_HOME/agents,
' which is where its subagent_paths point.
'
' So the image test goes THROUGH the entrypoint and asks the harness's own
' registry to load what it seeded, requiring exactly the roster _roster.json
' declares — READ FROM THE IMAGE rather than restated in the test, so a roster
' change cannot leave the assertion stale again.
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
title Subagent definition sharing — composed at container start, never duplicated

node "defs/subagents — the single source" as SRC <<host>> {
  component "<name>.md\nshared body, {{TOKEN}} placeholders" as BODY <<app>>
  component "_frontmatter/<harness>/<name>.yaml\nper-harness schema, verbatim" as FM <<app>>
  component "_vars/<harness>.env\ntoken values" as VARS <<app>>
}

component "render_subagents()\nin packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh" as RENDER <<app>>

node "composed at first run" as OUT <<host>> {
  component "~/.claude/agents · 5\ntools: · model:" as CC <<app>>
  component "cecli agents · 10\nmode: · permission:" as CE <<app>>
  component "opencode agents · 10\nmode: · permission:" as OC <<app>>
  component "~/.cursor/agents · 2\nreadonly:" as CU <<app>>
}

component "agents_shared_test.go\ncomposes via the same shell fn" as GUARD <<app>>
component "An image missing the shared dir" as DRIFT <<error>>

BODY ARROW_MAIN RENDER
FM ARROW_MAIN RENDER
VARS ARROW_MAIN RENDER
RENDER ARROW_MAIN CC
RENDER ARROW_MAIN CE
RENDER ARROW_MAIN OC
RENDER ARROW_MAIN CU
OUT ARROW_MAIN GUARD : asserted on composed output
GUARD ARROW_ERROR DRIFT : COPY asserted per Dockerfile

note top of BODY
  **One body, because the advice is one advice.**
  The four harnesses had drifted to four copies of
  the same document, and cecli and opencode were
  byte-identical for every agent they shared, so
  the duplication bought nothing at all.
end note

note bottom of FM
  **Frontmatter is the real difference.** Claude
  Code declares a ""tools"" allowlist and a model,
  opencode and cecli declare ""mode"" with a
  permission block, and cursor declares
  ""readonly"", so the schema cannot be shared.
end note

note bottom of VARS
  **Tokens carry the only prose that legitimately
  varies.** The orchestrator is called ""build""
  in opencode and the main agent in Claude Code,
  and a monorepo handoff can only name domain
  agents the receiving roster actually contains.
end note

note bottom of RENDER
  **Substitution is literal, never a regex.** The
  bodies are full of backticks, globs and path
  separators that a sed expression would mangle,
  so the renderer replaces tokens through bash
  parameter expansion instead.
end note

note top of OUT
  **Nothing composed is ever committed.** Each
  entrypoint joins the shared body to its own
  frontmatter at first run, so the repository
  holds one copy per agent and the image holds
  one shared directory rather than four.
end note

note bottom of GUARD
  **The guard shells out to the real function.**
  A Go reimplementation could agree with itself
  while disagreeing with the image, so the test
  composes through ""render_subagents"" and
  validates the definitions a container receives.
end note

@enduml
